From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: iertutil: Windows.Foundation.Uri takes a DOS path as a file: URI

On Windows, new Uri("C:\x\y.msix") is file:///C:/x/y.msix. winget hands
PackageManager the MSIX it downloaded that way; the Uri constructor
refused it (E_INVALIDARG) and every MSIX install from winget ended in
"0x80070057 : Invalid parameter". urlmon's CreateUri is now asked with
Uri_CREATE_ALLOW_IMPLICIT_FILE_SCHEME. A string that is neither an
absolute URI nor a path is still an invalid argument.

--- a/dlls/iertutil/main.c
+++ b/dlls/iertutil/main.c
@@ -421,8 +421,10 @@
     uri_impl->ref = 1;
 
     /* Windows.Foundation.Uri is always absolute: a string urlmon cannot
-     * parse as one is an invalid argument, as on Windows. */
-    if (FAILED(hr = CreateUri(raw, 0, 0, &uri_impl->uri)))
+     * parse as one is an invalid argument, as on Windows. A DOS or UNC path
+     * is a file: URI (C:\x -> file:///C:/x), as on Windows: programs pass
+     * downloaded files to PackageManager that way. */
+    if (FAILED(hr = CreateUri(raw, Uri_CREATE_ALLOW_IMPLICIT_FILE_SCHEME, 0, &uri_impl->uri)))
     {
         WARN("invalid uri %s, hr %#lx\n", debugstr_w(raw), hr);
         free(uri_impl);
